B = [
    ('Schwinn','North America','1950s-60s','bicycles','In the style of Schwinn, heavy, swooping, streamlined mid-century American forms that look fast even when standing still. Bodies swell into deep curves with a faux fuel-tank bulge and long sweeping arcs, balanced by fat wide wheels with cream white-wall rubber. Deep candy enamel in cherry red, turquoise, cream and black, edged with fine white pinstripes. Generous bright chrome on rims, lamps, bars and trim, with a tall chrome flourish at the rear. Wide, swept-back, relaxed shapes, plush padded seating and small playful tassels or fins. Jet-age optimism and showroom shine.'),
    ('Raleigh','Europe','1950s-70s','bicycles','In the style of Raleigh, sturdy, upright, practical British engineering with quiet dignity. Slim steel tubes in deep racing green, black or maroon in glossy enamel, with fine hand-lined gold pinstripes at the joints and a small enamelled badge showing a bird. Full chrome guards and mudguards, sprung brown leather with brass or copper rivets, cream grips and tall, upright proportions. Parts are exposed, honest and repairable, with a neat bell and lamp added as practical extras. Rugged, reliable, rain-ready, sensible English craftsmanship with a post-war countryside feel.'),
    ('Boeing','North America','1960s-present','aircraft','In the style of Boeing, clean, confident, bright aluminium-and-white American jet-age engineering. Long smooth tubular volumes with a gently rounded nose and a slightly raised forward bulge, wings swept back and carrying large cylindrical pods in white and silver. White upper surfaces over polished bare metal, a grey nose cone, one narrow deep blue stripe running the length of a tidy row of small round-cornered windows, and a tall tail fin carrying one large bold colour mark. Precise panel seams, crisp edges and white undercarriage hardware. Optimistic, orderly, dependable and modern.'),
    ('Airbus','Europe','1990s-present','aircraft','In the style of Airbus, smooth, calm, computer-drawn European modernism. A perfectly round tube body ending in a blunt, softly rounded nose, with dark glazing wrapped in a sleek black swoosh. Slim swept wings with upturned tips that curve skyward, large underslung round pods, and a tall fin in bold colour. Clean white livery with a restrained palette of blue and white, a neat line of small rounded windows and flush, seamless panels. Uncluttered, cool, efficient and quietly high-tech, with a gentle sense of digital precision.'),
    ('de Havilland','Europe','1930s-50s','aircraft','In the style of de Havilland, light, nimble, gracefully proportioned British forms of the 1930s to 1950s. Slim fuselages with smooth wooden curves, elliptical tails and curved cowlings that hug the engine. Wings of taut fabric in silver dope, with bright trainer yellow for contrast, and aluminium panels left bare and polished. Glazed bubble canopies, fish-like pod bodies on twin booms for the jet era, and simple round roundel marks in red, white and blue. Streamlined, clean and elegant, craftsman-built, with a hopeful pre-war and post-war amateur-flyer charm.'),
    ('Supermarine','Europe','1930s-40s','aircraft','In the style of Supermarine, sleek, purposeful British aerodynamic purity of the 1930s and 1940s. Graceful elliptical wings, a long slim nose, a tapered tail and a narrow stance, all in polished metal skin with flush rivets. Wartime camouflage in dark green and earth brown on top with pale sky blue below, bright round markings in red, white and blue, and, for racing, glossy blue and silver lacquer with long slender floats. A rounded bubble canopy and fine, thin lines. Fast-looking, elegant, lean and precise, pared down to speed alone.'),
    ('Cessna','North America','1960s-70s','aircraft','In the style of Cessna, friendly, simple, practical light-aircraft design from the 1960s and 1970s. A boxy but approachable white body with a strut-braced wing mounted high, large windows wrapping around the cabin, a tall angular tail and a two-bladed propeller with a small spinner. Wheels sit under streamlined fairings. Painted racing stripes sweep along the sides in red, blue, gold or green, with small neat registration numbers. Plain, honest shapes, easy to read, sturdy and unfussy, with a casual weekend-flyer optimism and a utility-first, general aviation feel.'),
    ('Sikorsky','North America','1950s-70s','helicopters','In the style of Sikorsky, rugged, heavy-duty, utilitarian rotary-wing machinery. A big rounded, bulbous nose with deep glazing, a tall central mast with thick blades, and a long tapering tail ending in a small rotor. Stubby side pods, large intake and exhaust fairings and riveted aluminium skin with visible fasteners. Paint is either matte olive drab and grey for military work, or white and red for rescue, with big black and white stencilled numbers and warnings. No ornament, everything functional, strong, workmanlike and built to lift and endure.'),
    ('Concorde','Europe','1970s','aircraft','In the style of Concorde, a needle-sharp, supersonic, futuristic elegance of the 1970s. A tall, slender white body narrowing to a long pointed nose that droops downward, with tiny oval windows in a slim line. A pure, smooth, ogival delta shape sweeps back into a tapered tail with a pointed cone, with engines tucked beneath in sharp rectangular housings. White paint is relieved only by one thin blue line along the sides. Knife-slim, bird-like, pared-back and aerodynamic, with a refined, rarefied air of speed and luxury.'),
    ('Kenworth','North America','1970s-present','trucks','In the style of Kenworth, proud, polished, long-nosed American heavy-duty highway presence. A tall, upright chrome grille set in a long flat sloping hood with bright chrome edge strips, big rectangular chrome mirrors, round lamps and a heavy chrome bumper with a visor over the windscreen. Two tall stainless stacks rise behind the cab. Deep two-tone paint split by a bold stripe, polished aluminium wheels and a roomy sleeper cab. Everything is gleaming, mirrored and meticulously cared for, with a bold, confident, king-of-the-road stance.'),
    ('Peterbilt','North America','1970s-present','trucks','In the style of Peterbilt, a showy, sculpted, long-nosed American heavy-duty look. A long, curved hood with a bold oval chrome grille, vertical louvres and rounded corners, a single round chrome-ringed headlamp in each fender, and curved sweeping fenders. A tall chrome stack, big chrome bumper, polished tank covers and a sleeper cab. Brilliant candy paint in black, red, blue or green is trimmed with fine pinstripes and gold lines. Classic, bold, polished and proud, with a strong highway stance and lots of mirror-bright metal.'),
    ('Scania','Europe','2000s-present','trucks','In the style of Scania, clean, crisp, modern Nordic engineering with a tall flat-fronted, upright face. A broad, wide grille crossed by one bold horizontal bar, narrow angular headlamps and a wide, tall windscreen. Rounded roof fairings with deflectors, a high-roof cabin, long side skirts and tidy lines that flow back along the body. A silver and blue crowned winged-beast emblem sits centred on the grille. Livery is tidy and solid, in white, red, blue or yellow, with no clutter. Rational, tidy, safe, practical and quietly premium.'),
    ('Mack Trucks','North America','1950s-present','trucks','In the style of Mack Trucks, blunt, tough, muscular American heavy-duty character. A bulldog-like nose, a hood that curves down steeply, and a bold chrome standing animal ornament on top. A stout upright chrome grille with horizontal bars, round chrome lamps, short heavy fenders, a thick chrome bumper and a stubby cab. Bright enamel in red, yellow, blue or black, with stainless stacks. Chunky, compact, solid and no-nonsense, proportioned like a determined fighter, with polished metal highlights on a hard-working frame.'),
    ('John Deere','North America','1950s-present','tractors','In the style of John Deere, robust, hard-working, clean agricultural design. Deep green bodywork with bright yellow rims and trim, forming one memorable two-colour pairing. A boxy hood with a vertical grille, a rounded fuel cap, large rear tyres with deep lugs, a tall exhaust stack and open or glazed operator areas. A bold leaping deer mark sits on the side in yellow. Simple yellow stripes and clean decals accent the green. Practical proportions, honest function, tidy, dependable and rooted in the countryside.'),
    ('Fendt','Europe','2000s-present','tractors','In the style of Fendt, premium, precise German farm engineering in glossy, bright lime green with matte black accents. High-polish paint, sleek rounded bonnet lines and sharply cut angular LED headlamp strips. A big glass cabin with a curved panoramic windscreen, a metallic silver and black grille with one wide horizontal slot, and minimal clutter across clean, tight bodywork. Large tyres and exact panel gaps suggest sharp machining. Modern, upmarket, tidy, high-tech and confident, like agricultural luxury.'),
    ('Massey Ferguson','Europe','1950s-70s','tractors','In the style of Massey Ferguson, plain, sturdy post-war farm machinery. Bright red bodywork with grey wheels, chassis and engine, a rounded bonnet with a vertical slatted grille, chunky rubber tyres with deep tread and an exposed exhaust pipe. A simple open seat with a basic steering wheel, or a small safety cab. Bold block lettering sits on the bonnet side. Two strong colours, red and grey, are used flat and simply. Honest, tough, utilitarian, no frills, and rooted in mid-century working farmland.'),
    ('Routemaster','Europe','1950s-60s','buses','In the style of Routemaster, nostalgic, rounded, sturdy London transport design. Deep pillar-box red paint with a cream or pale band between the two levels, a boxy body with big curved corners and a tall rounded front with a simple radiator-style grille. An open rear platform with a pole, large destination boxes above the windscreen, a roundel and fleet number on the side, and deep sliding windows. Route numbers use stencil-like, bold lettering. Civic, familiar, friendly and proudly old-fashioned.'),
    ('Greyhound','North America','1950s-60s','buses','In the style of Greyhound, optimistic mid-century American road-travel streamlining. A stainless steel body with long fluted, corrugated sides, a low rounded roof and large tinted windows. A destination sign sits above the windscreen, and a leaping dog silhouette appears in the side panels. Livery is blue and silver with white stripes. Polished aluminium panels, rounded fenders and a smooth, speed-minded profile. Shiny, practical, spacious, modern-for-its-time and full of highway confidence.'),
    ('Great Western Railway','Europe','1930s','railways','In the style of Great Western Railway, proud Victorian-inspired engineering elegance. Gleaming Brunswick green paint with orange and black lining on the cab and boiler, polished brass domes and valve covers, a copper-capped chimney, a black smokebox and a red buffer beam with number plates. Tall brass-edged nameplates sit on the wheel covers. Coaches are cream and chocolate brown. Metal is hand-polished, lines are fine and hand-drawn, and every part is crafted to be admired. Stately, dignified, traditional and richly finished.'),
    ('Shinkansen','East Asia','1960s-present','railways','In the style of Shinkansen, calm, ultra-precise, aerodynamic Japanese high-speed modernity. A long, smooth, continuous body ending in a duck-bill or beak-shaped nose, with a rounded cross-section and flush windows and doors. White bodywork carries one thin blue or colour stripe along the windows. A narrow wraparound cab window, low skirts hiding the running gear, and near-seamless, polished surfaces. Quiet, futuristic, tidy and disciplined, where every curve serves speed and silence.'),
    ('TGV','Europe','1980s','railways','In the style of TGV, sleek, French, wedge-shaped, high-speed modernism of the 1980s. A pointed, sloped nose with a small oval windscreen set deep in the front, a long tapering roof and tightly articulated slim body. Livery is orange and silver-grey, with a bold orange belly and a dark grey roof. Windows are flush, surfaces are smooth, and the profile is low, streamlined and futuristic. Confident, athletic, sporty, sharply tailored and engineered for speed.'),
    ('Orient Express','Europe','1920s-30s','railways','In the style of Orient Express, opulent, romantic 1920s-30s luxury travel. Deep royal blue panels with gold lettering and fine gold lining, a rounded barrel roof and polished brass handrails. Interiors glow with glossy varnished teak and mahogany, marquetry panels, brass luggage racks, burgundy velvet seating, crisp white table linen, crystal and silver. Art deco lamps have frosted glass tulip shades. Everything is lacquered, gilded and carefully made. Atmosphere is glamorous, intimate, mysterious and unhurried.'),
    ('Riva','Europe','1960s','boats','In the style of Riva, glamorous, glossy Italian Riviera luxury of the 1960s. A long, slim, low hull in deep mahogany, with a varnished deck in bright caramel grain, finished to mirror gloss. Curved, polished chrome frames, chrome cleats and fittings, white leather or cream and red upholstery, and fine white or gold pinstripes. A swept stern, a rounded rear deck and a small flagstaff. Handmade, sensual, sleek, sunlit and richly refined, with a jet-set summer feel.'),
    ('Chris-Craft','North America','1930s-50s','boats','In the style of Chris-Craft, classic, varnished, lakeside summer glamour in the 1930s-50s American tradition. Rich red-brown mahogany planking polished to a deep shine, with fine white caulked seams between boards. Chrome-framed windscreens, chrome cleats and lights, a slim chine and a rounded transom with a script nameplate. Tufted leather seating in red and cream, and neatly curved cockpits. Handcrafted, warm, nostalgic, sporty and carefree, like long sunny weekends on calm water.'),
    ('Sunseeker','Europe','2000s-present','boats','In the style of Sunseeker, sleek, low, sporty British luxury. A raked, aggressive forward slope, a long white glossy hull and deck, and dark tinted wraparound glazing. Bold swooping stripes sweep along the sides, with polished stainless rails and teak-clad decks. Upper levels have sunpads and loungers. Interiors are lacquered in cream leather and high-gloss wood. Speed-minded, status-conscious, polished and flamboyant, with a high-glamour marina look and a cool white palette.'),
    ('Boston Whaler','North America','1960s-present','boats','In the style of Boston Whaler, honest, tough, practical, unsinkable simplicity. Wide, stable, twin-hull forms in white gelcoat with a thin navy or blue stripe at the waterline and a high flared bow. A simple centre console with a stainless rail and leaning post, grey non-slip decks, a small helm, and a motor on a bracket at the rear. Rod holders and cleats are neatly bolted on. No fuss, no ornament, durable, utilitarian, ready for work or play, with a straightforward coastal feel.'),
    ('NASA','North America','1960s-70s','spacecraft','In the style of NASA, clean, technical, optimistic American spaceflight of the 1960s and 1970s. Tall white forms with bold black roll patterns, small flags in red, white and blue, and golden foil-wrapped conical shapes. Bright white suits with orange or silver details. Logo styles are either a red worm-like lettering or a blue circle with stars and a swoosh. Riveted aluminium panels, dark glossy heat shields, exposed cabling and engine bells, all against black space. Engineered, heroic, hopeful and precise.'),
    ('SpaceX','North America','2010s-present','spacecraft','In the style of SpaceX, minimalist, gleaming, modern reusable spaceflight. Smooth white cylinders with clean bold finishes, or polished bare stainless steel, with slender black legs and a black interstage. Engine sections are sooty and streaked with carbon from fiery returns. A rounded nose, slim grid fins, a tapered capsule with a black heat shield and minimal bold sans-serif lettering. Few marks, no ornament, only function. Sleek, futuristic, confident, utilitarian and quietly daring.'),
    ('Soviet space programme','Russia and Eastern Europe','1960s','spacecraft','In the style of Soviet space programme, blunt, heavy, utilitarian 1960s industrial heroism. A round spherical capsule with portholes, bare pea green and metallic silver hulls, a cluster of tapering boosters hugging a central core, and brushed orange-tinted foil. White sections carry stencilled numbers, with bold red capital lettering and a red star or hammer-like mark. Visible cables, rivets and welded seams. Raw, practical, monumental, heavy-engineered and undecorated, with a stern, proud Cold War mood.'),
    ('Pullman','North America','1900s-30s','railways','In the style of Pullman, formal Gilded Age elegance in luxury rail travel of the early 1900s. Deep dark green paint with elaborate gold-leaf lettering and lines along the sides, an arched roof with small high windows, and a rear platform with a railing. Interiors in walnut with green or burgundy plush upholstery, brass fittings and gaslight-style lamps. Heavy steel-clad bodies are solid and stately. Ornate, rich, ceremonial, hand-gilded and imposing, like a rolling grand hotel.'),
    ('Piaggio Ape','Europe','1950s-60s','trucks','In the style of Piaggio Ape, tiny, quaint, cheerful Italian village practicality. A rounded cab on three wheels with one at the front, scooter-style handlebars or a small bench seat, and a small tin cargo bed behind. Pressed-steel body in pastel mint, cream, light blue or sun-faded yellow, with rounded fenders, a tiny windscreen and chrome trim around a single headlamp. Simple, humble, charming, slightly worn and friendly, built for narrow lanes and daily errands.'),
    ('Zeppelin','Europe','1920s-30s','aircraft','In the style of Zeppelin, stately, monumental, silver-giant 1920s-30s elegance. An enormous cigar-shaped hull stretched taut over a light frame, covered in silvery aluminium-doped cloth, with a small streamlined gondola underneath and rows of windows. Four cruciform tail fins, engine pods on struts and bold black Gothic lettering along the hull, plus a red flag on the tail. Smooth, gleaming, serene and huge, with a majestic, floating, slow-moving presence and a dignified period grandeur.'),
    ('Noritake','East Asia','1910s-1930s','ceramics','In the style of Noritake, refined, ornate, glittering early twentieth century export porcelain. Glossy bone-white glaze with a faint bluish translucency, formal shapes with scalloped edges, closed loop handles and small thumb curls, and lids topped by bud or fruit finials. Hand-painted and gilded decoration with wide borders of heavy gold, cobalt blue and deep rose red, central scenic panels in sunset orange and teal, and moriage dots and beads of enamel standing proud like raised pearls. Later Art Deco versions turn angular, with stepped triangles, black and orange bands, fans, sunbursts and pearly rainbow lustre. A small green or magenta stamped mark on the underside. Slightly nostalgic, treasured and cabinet-worthy.'),
    ('Shiseido','East Asia','1910s-1930s','cosmetics','In the style of Shiseido, luxurious, feminine, carefully composed Taisho and early Showa elegance where Art Nouveau curves meet Art Deco geometry. Slim, faceted glass shapes with domed stoppers, gilt metal caps, and lacquer red or ivory boxes tied with ribbon. Graphics use a stylised camellia-like flower mark in white or gold on red, thin hand-drawn lettering in an Art Nouveau block script, sinuous floral borders and flat-colour illustrations of slender women with swept-up hair, in muted rose, jade green, indigo and warm cream. Glossy surfaces with gold foil edging and delicate line work, soft monochrome theatrical photography, and generous empty margins around small precise motifs.'),
    ('Zojirushi','East Asia','1970s-present','appliances','In the style of Zojirushi, gentle, practical, trustworthy Japanese domestic design. Plump rounded forms with soft corners in cream white, pearl grey or brushed stainless steel, with a single dark glass or black panel carrying a small pale green backlit display and simple rounded buttons. Slim cylinders in satin steel or soft pastel enamel, flip-top push lids, sturdy folding handles. The mark is a small side-view elephant silhouette beside a red or black wordmark in friendly rounded letters. Surfaces are matte or satin, never flashy, with fine seams and tidy gaskets. Instruction icons are tiny line pictograms. Clean, quietly cheerful and reassuringly well made.'),
    ('Tamiya','East Asia','1970s-1980s','toys','In the style of Tamiya, precise, enthusiastic, sunny hobbyist modelmaking of the 1970s and 1980s. Packaging shows one subject painted in rich illustrated realism on a plain white background, with crisp edges, glossy highlights, believable dirt, rust and exhaust staining, and dramatic low angles, framed by a thin black border and a small two-star red and blue logo with clean black, red and blue sans-serif lettering. Parts sit on pale grey, olive or black plastic frames with sharp rivets, hexagonal bolt heads, fine panel lines and neat decals in white, red and yellow. Translucent shells are painted from inside in bright racing red, yellow and white with big stripes and number roundels, over chunky tyres, silver aluminium parts and exposed black chassis. Tidy exploded line drawings.'),
    ('Kewpie','East Asia','1925-present','food','In the style of Kewpie, cute, wholesome, babyish and nostalgic Japanese food branding built around a chubby baby mascot. Soft squeeze forms in clear or translucent white plastic with a bright red cap and a star-shaped opening that makes fine ridged lines. Labels are mostly white with a red wordmark and a small round doll figure with a cheerful face, wide-set eyes, rosy cheeks, plump belly, tiny wings and a single curled tuft of hair, drawn in simple flat outline with pink and cream fill. Older containers have tin lids and blue and red paper labels. Net-like orange-red cross-hatched lattice patterns appear. Pale yellow backgrounds, egg-yolk golds and fresh produce in neat circles, a limited red, yellow and white palette and a clean modern food-photograph finish.'),
    ('Yakult','East Asia','1960s-present','food','In the style of Yakult, clean, bright, hygienic, friendly miniature drink packaging. A squat pale plastic vessel about the size of a thumb joint, with a rounded shoulder, a ribbed faceted waist like a small cut-glass tumbler, and a wide mouth sealed by thin foil in white with red print. A glossy white wrap carries a bold red wordmark, a soft pink and blue accent band, a small drop motif and tiny black fine print. Contents are pale milky peach. Items are bundled in tight multipacks in printed paper sleeves, or lined in rows so the red and white pattern repeats. Carts and boxes are white and pale pink. Plenty of white, one hot red accent and a mild medical-nutrition feeling.'),
    ('Nissin Foods','East Asia','1970s-1980s','food','In the style of Nissin Foods, cheap, fast, fun, nostalgic 1970s-80s instant food packaging. Saturated, appetising, slightly garish colour in hot red, mustard yellow, black and white. Tall wide-mouthed foamed white cups with printed wraps, big italic chunky lettering in red outlined in white or black, shiny metallic film bags striped in red and yellow, and thick sans-serif titles slanting upward. Bright photos or illustrations of steaming food with shrimp, egg and green onion, a peel-back foil lid, a round window showing golden crimped noodles, and starburst flashes shouting new or tasty. Late-night convenience-store shelf energy.'),
    ('Tomica','East Asia','1970s-1980s','toys','In the style of Tomica, tidy, bright, practical, collectable and slightly retro miniature diecast design. Small metal bodies in one glossy solid enamel colour such as white, red, yellow, light blue or metallic silver, with clear plastic glazing, silver painted bumpers and lamps, tiny printed badges and hinged doors that really open. Chrome five-spoke hubs on small black tyres. Everyday vehicles keep real-world livery with painted stripes and lettering. Window boxes are cardboard sleeves with a picture window, black with yellow flaps, later red and white, with an illustrated action scene, white sans-serif model name and a number tab. Foreign models get blue and white boxes with a small flag.'),
    ('Namco','East Asia','1980s','games','In the style of Namco, cheerful, bouncy, golden-age arcade charm of the early 1980s. Characters are simple round shapes with big expressive eyes, drawn in a chunky low-resolution pixel grid on pure black. A yellow circle with a wedge mouth chases glowing dots through a neon blue outlined maze of rounded corridors, pursued by pastel ghosts in red, pink, cyan and orange with wavy skirts and blinking white eyes. Bonus fruit appears in flat bright pixel art. Symmetrical insect-like invaders in blue, purple and yellow dive in formation against single twinkling stars. Cabinets are upright boxes with cartoon side art, a slanted black marquee with a rounded glowing logo, a tilted screen with scanlines, a ball-top joystick and a few round buttons. Limited saturated colours, hard pixel edges.'),
    ('Korg','East Asia','1970s-1980s','instruments','In the style of Korg, functional, technical, compact, precise late 1970s and 1980s electronic design with a futuristic hi-fi flavour. Long, shallow wedge shapes with a slanted metal control panel in brushed or anodised charcoal and silver, covered in rows of small round knobs, chunky slider caps and tiny lever switches in orange, red, blue and white. Labels are screen-printed in clean white or orange sans-serif capitals with thin line diagrams of waves and signal routing, and a row of sockets at the upper left. Side cheeks are dark stained wood or black vinyl. Keys are cream white and matte black, square-edged. Small red LED digits and amber or green indicators glow. Compact grey boxes with rows of tiny rectangular rubber pads. Cool grey digital workstation mood.'),
    ('Kubota','East Asia','1960s-present','machinery','In the style of Kubota, sturdy, dependable, tidy and slightly cheerful machinery in a single unmistakable colour scheme. Body panels are bright safety orange in glossy even enamel over dark grey or black chassis, wheel centres and engine covers. Short rounded noses with slatted grilles, rectangular work lights, slim chrome stacks, flat step platforms and high-backed black seats under canopies or glass cabs with big wraparound windows. Deep chevron-treaded rubber. The mark is a white capital wordmark on an orange rectangle, with a thin grey band along the side, small white model numbers and yellow and black warning decals. Boxy booms, black rubber tracks and bright steel. Like well-maintained equipment resting in a green field.'),
    ('Asics','East Asia','1970s-1980s','footwear','In the style of Asics, athletic, light, vintage, understated, slightly nerdy-cool 1970s-80s Japanese performance design. Low, sleek forms in smooth suede mixed with light nylon mesh, a slightly flared heel and a gently curved toe. Two crossed diagonal stripes in a contrasting colour run along the side, usually white on navy, or red, yellow and blue on pale grey, with a thin scalloped overlay near the laces. Thick wedges of cream or white foam sit over crepe or waffle-patterned gum rubber. Earthy sporty colourways such as cream with burgundy, navy with sky blue, or grey with orange and lime. Small chunky italic white wordmarks with an Olympic-era retro feel.'),
    ('Calpis','East Asia','1950s-present','food','In the style of Calpis, clean, fresh, summery, childlike, retro design built on a polka dot pattern. An even field of round white dots on a rich blue ground, standing for a starry Milky Way, sometimes inverted to blue dots on white. A bold simple wordmark sits in a rounded white or blue rectangle in a soft rounded sans-serif. Tall slim shapes with narrow necks, wrapped in thin paper labels bearing the dots, or the same pattern at a larger scale with a glossy finish. Cloudy white contents, ice, a straw and a pale blue ribbon of colour behind. Flavour variants shift accents to orange, peach and green but keep the dots. Limited blue and white palette, gentle geometry.'),
    ('Citizen Watch','East Asia','1980s-2010s','watches','In the style of Citizen Watch, reliable, modern, understated, engineered and quietly elegant Japanese precision. Round or slightly cushion shapes in brushed and polished stainless steel or titanium, with a flat sapphire crystal and a slim bezel. Clean legible dials in silver white, deep navy, black or champagne, with applied baton markers, sharp sword-shaped hands with pale luminous fill, a small date window at three and a fine printed minute track. Sporty variants add a rotating bezel with alternating smooth and serrated sections, bold luminous dots and rugged bracelets. Dress versions use lacquered black, mother-of-pearl or paper-textured white with raised star or moon motifs. Brushed centre links with polished edges. Tidy thin capital text, cool metallic shine, lit from above.'),
    ('Taiwan Beer','East Asia','1970s-present','drinks','In the style of Taiwan Beer, cheerful, social, straightforward and hot-evening, with strong green, gold and white colour blocking. Brown glass with a white and green paper label bearing a small crest-like emblem, a bold sans-serif wordmark and a golden ring of wheat. Premium versions switch to gold and white, a medal version uses green glass with white, red and green. Metal containers carry white with blue stripes and green lettering, or glossy gold, blue and white. Imagery includes ears of malted barley, a gleaming gold medal rosette and foam-topped glasses against a plain pale ground. Log-cabin style halls with wooden beams, long benches, round tables and neon green signs.'),
    ('Kweichow Moutai','East Asia','1950s-present','drinks','In the style of Kweichow Moutai, formal, festive, prosperous and traditional ceremonial design. A squat cylindrical white porcelain flask with a short neck, glossy milk-white glaze and a slight shoulder curve, topped with a red ribbon tied over a wax or plastic seal and often a tiny hanging tag. A bright vermilion label wraps the middle, edged in gold, with large black or gold brush-style characters and a flowing line of small text. Special editions use red glaze, blue and white, or glossy black. Gift boxes are lacquer red hard cartons or wood, lined with yellow silk, embossed in gold and closed with a white cord or golden bow, with small cups alongside. Auspicious red, gold and white against dark polished tables.'),
    ('Flying Pigeon','East Asia','1960s-1980s','vehicles','In the style of Flying Pigeon, utilitarian, durable, plain, communal and nostalgic mid-century Chinese roadster design. Black enamelled steel diamond frames, with a double top tube on the gents form or a low step-through loop on the ladies form. Large 28 inch wheels with chrome rims and thin spokes, a full-cover chain guard, a black rear rack with a leather pad, mudguards ending in pale cream tips and rod-operated brakes. Black leather saddle on big coil springs, wide upright sweeping bars with black grips. White pinstripes and gold-lined transfers, a stylised dove head badge, and thick cream-walled or black tyres. Muted monochrome palette of black, chrome and cream, seen in long dense rows.'),
    ('White Rabbit Creamy Candy','East Asia','1950s-present','food','In the style of White Rabbit Creamy Candy, sweet, nostalgic, modest, childlike old Shanghai charm. Plump cream-coloured rectangles wrapped in a thin edible rice paper film, then in waxed paper twisted and printed in white with red, blue and black hand lettering in both Chinese characters and Latin script. A naturalistic ink drawing of a white rabbit stands before an old-fashioned artist palette, drawn with fine line shading in the manner of 1950s commercial art. Outer packs are flat sealed pouches or bright red and white boxes with a large rabbit face, wide forward-looking eyes, a cartoonish cheerful animal on a pale blue sky ground. Display tins show vintage Art Deco borders. Limited white, red, blue and black palette with a slightly matte print texture.'),
    ('Tong Ren Tang','East Asia','Qing dynasty to present','retail','In the style of Tong Ren Tang, imperial, scholarly, aromatic, sombre and prosperous, like an old apothecary of lacquer, brass and paper. Long dark wooden lattice facades with carved eaves, lacquered red pillars, a horizontal black board with large gold brush calligraphy, tall hanging vertical signs and red paper lanterns. Interiors have floor-to-ceiling rows of small dark wood drawers with brass pulls and ink-labelled white tags, a high counter with a brass scale and abacus, and glass jars of dried roots and flowers. Packaging uses imperial yellow, vermilion red and gold with embossed dragon or lotus borders, round wax shells stamped with a small seal, traditional calligraphic characters and red seal stamps.'),
    ('Cathay Pacific','East Asia','1970s-2010s','airlines','In the style of Cathay Pacific, calm, urbane, polished, glassy and well-travelled design in green and white. A clean white body with a thin jade green line running under the windows, a dark green tail and a calligraphic brush-stroke emblem like a swept bird wing curving upward in white or pale green. An earlier version used lettuce green and white two-tone with bare metal. Titles are in an upright dark green sans-serif wordmark with small simple Chinese script beside it. Interiors are quiet, with warm timber-toned panels, bottle green seats with pale head covers, soft cream leather and thin gold accents. Crisp dark green uniforms with neat scarves and small gold wing pins. Harbour skyline at dusk.'),
    ('Hong Kong Tramways','East Asia','1950s-present','transport','In the style of Hong Kong Tramways, busy, nostalgic, neon-lit, crowded city transport. Tall, slim, upright boxy bodies with two storeys of tall rectangular windows in slim frames, a slightly curved roof, a short pole on top and open balcony fronts upstairs. Lower body in deep forest green with a cream or pale yellow stripe along the window line, and a square destination box with white characters on black. The most distinctive sight is the full-body advertising wrap in saturated colours, glossy photographs and bold Chinese and English lettering that covers the entire flank, so each vehicle becomes a rolling poster. Interiors have wooden slatted seats, brass handrails, a plain bell cord and wooden floors.'),
    ('Star Ferry','East Asia','1950s-present','transport','In the style of Star Ferry, leisurely, nostalgic, salty and civic harbour charm. Low, broad hulls with a rounded overhanging bow, a white upper cabin and a narrow upper deck with a canvas or wooden awning, ringed by a thin white railing. Hull and trim in deep bottle green below clean white upperworks, with a gold rubbing strake, black funnel top, brass fittings and cream life rings. Names in white Latin letters and Chinese characters appear on the bow. Slatted wooden benches flip to face either way. Interiors show creamy paint, rows of varnished timber seats and round portholes. Piers are green steel sheds with clock towers. Skyscrapers behind, hazy sky and dark teal water.'),
    ('Din Tai Fung','East Asia','2000s-present','food','In the style of Din Tai Fung, meticulous, hygienic, bustling and warm, with an exacting clean presentation. Small steamed parcels with paper-thin translucent skins, each gathered by hand into a tidy spiral of fine pleats with a little knot at the top, sitting in a round bamboo steamer with glints of broth showing. Open glass-walled kitchens show white-uniformed cooks in caps, masks and gloves under bright white light, rolling dough on stainless steel tables and weighing each piece on small scales. Modern dining rooms have pale oak tables, blond wood screens, red brushed lettering signs, dark slate floors and slatted lanterns. Tiny dishes of black vinegar with sliced ginger. Palette of cream, bamboo tan, steam white and one red accent.'),
    ('Lee Kum Kee','East Asia','1900s-present','food','In the style of Lee Kum Kee, trusted, family-run, festive and old-fashioned heritage labelling with dense decoration. Clear bottles with a short neck, a red screw cap and a wide wraparound paper label in rich red with gold border lines. A circular central picture of a woman and a boy on a small flat boat on a river, drawn in a simplified storybook engraving with fine black outline and flat gold, green and cream fills, surrounded by the name in big golden brush strokes and Latin capitals. A gold ribbon banner and a small seal stamp repeat across the range. Gift tins are red square cans with gold lettering and traditional pattern borders. Glossy dark brown contents, food shots with wok flames and shiny glazed meats.'),
    ('Li-Ning','East Asia','2000s-present','fashion','In the style of Li-Ning, energetic, patriotic, confident, youthful sportswear with bold national flavour mixing retro sports nostalgia and streetwear flair. A red geometric stroke like a flowing check mark or abstract athlete over bold red Chinese characters, often on white or black. Strong colour blocks of imperial red, black, white and metallic gold, with big rectangle patches and block lettering on the chest. Chunky midsoles with visible cushioning pods, bold geometric panels and ornate dragon-scale texture. Stand collars, broad contrast stripes down the arms and legs, glossy nylon and retro 1990s team colours in red, yellow and green. Fashion pieces add calligraphy, cloud and dragon motifs, brocade panels and oversize shapes. Bright red signage with white text.'),
    ('Nongshim','East Asia','1980s-present','food','In the style of Nongshim, bold, hot, hearty, no-nonsense and late-night convenience-store feel. Deep red and black packaging with a big photograph of glossy noodles in fiery red broth with floating slices of green onion, egg yolk and mushroom, set against a dark matte background. Titles are in heavy white and yellow Korean characters with a strong brush-like edge and a small character in a red square seal. A bright flame graphic and hot chilli accent signal spiciness. Cup versions use a black and red wrap with a peel-back foil lid. The corporate mark is a small seed-shaped logo with an arc in red and green. Snack bags in orange and yellow with cartoon accents. Saturated red, black and golden yellow.'),
    ('Gentle Monster','East Asia','2010s-present','eyewear','In the style of Gentle Monster, playful, futuristic, uncanny, theatrical and avant-garde. Oversized, sculptural frames in chunky glossy black, tortoise brown, milky translucent grey or pale pink, with thick geometric rims, rounded squares, cat-eye wings and big wraparound shields. Metal bridges in silver or gold with fine hinges, and tinted lenses in blue, green, orange or mirror gradient. Small engraved logo marks in tiny white capitals. Spaces are more art gallery than shop, with huge kinetic sculptures, robotic arms, animal-like figures, towering mirrored walls, glowing plant-like installations and surreal landscapes of foam, resin, concrete and silicone in stark white or black, with a single object placed like an artefact on a plinth. Moody, dramatically lit photography against odd backdrops.'),
    ('Korean Air','East Asia','1984-2024','airlines','In the style of Korean Air, orderly, polite, spacious, corporate and sky-high, with cool blue colours and a clean white body under a cloudless sky. A white lower body and a sky blue upper stripe over a wide silver-grey line, with a big round emblem of swirling red and blue halves twisting around each other on the tail. The title is a bold, rounded serif wordmark in light blue, in a heavy slab-like cut with quirky character. A later redesign shifts to a dark navy outlined emblem and a tidy sans-serif. Interiors in calm light blue and grey with white head cloths, warm wood-toned panels and cream carpeting. Light blue and white uniforms with neat scarves and pale gloves.'),
    ('Lotte Confectionery','East Asia','1960s-present','food','In the style of Lotte Confectionery, cute, light, childlike and refreshing, with flat colour, bold outlines, whimsical animals and a nostalgic convenience-store candy shelf. Slim mint green or cool blue sleeves with a cartoon penguin on an iceberg wearing a tiny bow tie, drawn in smooth outline with a bright white belly. Small hexagonal boxes in pastel blue and white with a round-eyed koala mascot in a different pose on each pack, and cream-filled bear-shaped biscuits with a printed face. Rich red, gold and brown foil wrappers with an embossed curved wordmark. Thin tubes and bright boxes in orange, yellow and green with playful bouncing type. Glossy, graphic and clear surfaces.'),
    ('Amul','South Asia','1960s-present','food','In the style of Amul, witty, homey, playful, everyday-Indian and nostalgic, painted in mural style on wall and street. Small rectangular foil-wrapped blocks in yellow with a red band, a bold red wordmark in rounded sans-serif capitals with a thick outline, and a little girl mascot with a blue polka dot dress, a red bow in blue-green hair, a button nose and a cheeky smile, drawn in clean cartoon ink lines. Posters in yellow or sky blue pair a witty cartoon with a bold hand-lettered headline in white or red on a stripe, a slab of buttered toast beneath, and a tiny red logo tag in the corner. Flat poster-paint colour in strong saturated red, yellow, blue and white. Hand-painted, jaunty, slightly uneven lettering. Glossy blue and white pouches.'),
    ('Bajaj Auto','South Asia','1970s-1990s','vehicles','In the style of Bajaj Auto, cheerful, unpretentious, resilient and familiar, packed with colour and rattle on a dusty street. Rounded pressed-steel bodies with a bulbous front mudguard, a curved leg shield, a bench seat with vinyl cover and a small spare wheel on the side panel. Thick glossy enamel in sky blue, cream, off-white, rust red and olive green, with chrome side badges, a round chrome-rimmed headlamp and a stubby upright mirror. Tiny three-wheelers with a canvas or sheet metal cab, open sides and a black fold-down hood, in lemon yellow and black, or green and yellow, with a black bench seat, painted slogans and plastic flower garlands.'),
]
